Windows Registry Editor Version 5.00

; USB selective-suspend power management off
; Source: MaxxTopia catalog (process.usb-power-mgmt.disable, mechanism tier)
; Stops Windows from entering selective-suspend on USB hub devices.
; Removes the 1-3ms wake stalls that hit when a sleeping USB controller
; is needed mid-frame.
; Registry: HKLM\SYSTEM\CurrentControlSet\Services\usbhub\Parameters\EnhancedPowerManagementEnabled
; Value 0 = enhanced power management disabled. Default = key absent.
; Reboot required: yes
; Revert: delete the EnhancedPowerManagementEnabled value

[HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\SYSTEM\CurrentControlSet\Services\usbhub\Parameters]
"EnhancedPowerManagementEnabled"=dword:00000000
